course: dictionary
lesson: 11608
title: Shared out and blamed: apportioned
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Apportioned is a formal word. It is the past form of apportion, and it means shared out or divided among people, usually in fair or set parts. «The money was apportioned equally among four children.» The word equally tells you each child got the same amount.
explain: Apportioned can also be about blame or responsibility. «The judge apportioned blame to the driver who broke the rule.» Here, the judge gave a share of the blame to the driver, so apportioned means given out as a share.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler word, such as shared out or divided. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Try it with «The money was shared out equally among four children.» It works.
fact: Apportioned means shared out or divided among people, often in fair or set parts.
fact: Apportioned can also mean gave a share of blame or responsibility to someone.
fact: Apportion is the base word. Its other forms are apportions, apportioning and apportioned.
fact: «Apportioned equally» means shared out in exactly equal parts.
fact: «Apportion blame» means to decide how much blame each person should get.
exercise: «The money was apportioned equally among four children.» What does apportioned mean here? | Lost in the park | Given back to the bank | *Shared out in equal parts | Spent all at once
exercise: «The judge apportioned blame to the driver who broke the rule.» What was given out? | A new car | A prize for good driving | A map of the town | *A share of the blame
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as apportioned? | *divided | painted | empty | forgotten
test: «The teacher apportioned the twelve pencils between the two groups.» What does this mean? | The pencils were broken in half | *The pencils were shared out between the groups | The pencils were given to the head teacher only | The pencils were lost in the classroom
test: «Twelve sweets were apportioned equally among 3 friends.» How many sweets does each friend get? | 36 | *4 | 2 | 9
exam: «The report apportioned blame for the delay between the bus company and the council.» What does the report do? | It pays for the new buses | It stops the bus from running | It says the delay was nobody's fault | *It gives a share of the blame to each one
